From: Topeet <support@topeet.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 15:25:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] videocrop: Support NV24 through the planar crop path

RK3588 HDMI RX delivers YUV 4:4:4 as NV24. CameraBin inserts videocrop
after v4l2src, but videocrop only classifies NV12 and NV21 as supported
semi-planar formats. This makes the CameraBin viewfinder fail with
not-negotiated even after V4L2 has correctly opened the device.

NV24 has a full-height interleaved UV plane, so it must use the generic
planar crop routine rather than the NV12-specific semi-planar routine,
which assumes vertically subsampled chroma. The generic routine already
uses GstVideoFormatInfo's plane strides and subsampling factors.

Signed-off-by: Topeet <support@topeet.com>
---
 gst/videocrop/gstvideocrop.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gst/videocrop/gstvideocrop.c b/gst/videocrop/gstvideocrop.c
--- a/gst/videocrop/gstvideocrop.c
+++ b/gst/videocrop/gstvideocrop.c
@@ -900,6 +900,10 @@ gst_video_crop_set_info (GstVideoFilter * vfilter, GstCaps * in,
     case GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_Y41B:
       crop->packing = VIDEO_CROP_PIXEL_FORMAT_PLANAR;
       break;
+    case GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV24:
+      /* NV24 has a full-height UV plane; use format-aware plane copying. */
+      crop->packing = VIDEO_CROP_PIXEL_FORMAT_PLANAR;
+      break;
     case GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV12:
     case GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_NV21:
       crop->packing = VIDEO_CROP_PIXEL_FORMAT_SEMI_PLANAR;
